    "raw": "Let's denote Luna's house rental budget as \\( R \\) and her food budget as \\( F \\). According to the problem, Luna's food budget is 60% of her house rental budget, so we can write:\n\\[ F = 0.6R \\]\n\nThe total budget for house rental and food is $240, so:\n\\[ R + F = 240 \\]\n\nSubstituting \\( F = 0.6R \\) into the equation \\( R + F = 240 \\):\n\\[ R + 0.6R = 240 \\]\n\\[ 1.6R = 240 \\]\n\\[ R = \\frac{240}{1.6} \\]\n\\[ R = 150 \\]\n\nNow, substituting \\( R = 150 \\) back into the equation \\( F = 0.6R \\):\n\\[ F = 0.6 \\times 150 \\]\n\\[ F = 90 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find Luna's phone bill budget, which is 10% of her food budget:\n\\[ \\text{Phone bill} = 0.1F \\]\n\\[ \\text{Phone bill} = 0.1 \\times 90 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Phone bill} = 9 \\]\n\nFinally, we sum up all the expenses to find Luna's total monthly budget:\n\\[ \\text{Total monthly budget} = R + F + \\text{Phone bill} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total monthly budget} = 150 + 90 + 9 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total monthly budget} = 249 \\]\n\nThus, Luna's total monthly budget to pay all these expenses is 249.\n\nFINAL: 249",
